-- Where a job's finished clip actually came from.
--
-- Until now every output was generated by the video model, so there was nothing to record. Two
-- repairs change that: a clip whose tail was extended (the original picture plus added seconds and
-- the full dialogue laid over both) and a clip the creator produced themselves and uploaded.
--
-- Worth recording rather than inferring. A shot that was repaired looks identical in every other
-- column -- same job, same prompt, same cost -- and someone reading the table later has no way to
-- tell why its duration no longer matches what was dispatched. It also stops a re-render quietly
-- discarding hand-finished work without anyone noticing what was lost.
ALTER TABLE video_gen_job ADD COLUMN output_origin VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'GENERATED';
